21485621,2026-04-22,Debt collection,Credit card debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt was paid,"To Whom It May Concern, I am submitting this statement to file a formal complaint regarding the collection activities of LVNV Funding LLC. 

LVNV Funding LLC contacted me on XXXX XXXX, 2026, attempting to collect a debt allegedly associated with my XXXX XXXX XXXX credit card account. However, this account remains in hands of the original creditor, and I am currently making payments directly to the original creditor, XXXX XXXX. Based on this, I dispute the validity of LVNV Funding LLCs claim that this debt is owed to them. 

Given that the account is still with the original creditor, not sold, or transferred, and remains with the original creditor, LVNV Funding LLC does not appear to have a legitimate basis to collect on this account. Their actions raise serious concerns about inaccurate reporting and improper collection practices. 

Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), I have the right to dispute inaccurate or incomplete information on my credit report. Any furnisher of information is required to ensure that the data they report is accurate and verifiable. Reporting a debt that is not owed, duplicated, or still being paid to the original creditor may constitute a violation of the FCRA. 

Additionally, under the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ), debt collectors are prohibited from attempting to collect debts that are not valid or that they can not substantiate. Continued contact regarding a disputed and potentially invalid debt may also violate federal law. 

Therefore, I am formally requesting the following : That LVNV Funding LLC immediately cease all communication with me regarding this matter. 
That LVNV Funding LLC provide proper validation of the alleged debt, including proof of ownership and transfer, if they claim it is valid. 
That LVNV Funding LLC permanently remove and delete any negative or inaccurate reporting related to this account from all three major credit reporting agencies if they can not validate the debt. 

Please consider this a formal dispute and request for investigation. I expect that this matter will be handled in accordance with all applicable federal laws and consumer protection regulations. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX",,Resurgent Capital Services L.P.,IL,60473,,Web,2026-04-22,Closed with explanation,Yes
