3. Proof of Legal OwnershipProvide evidence that you are the lawful owner of this specific account and have the legal right to collect.

4. Forward Flow Agreement ( if applicable ) If you rely on any forward flow agreement, provide documentation demonstrating how my specific account is included, as such agreements alone do not establish ownership of individual accounts.

5. Authority to ReportProvide proof of your permissible purpose and authority to furnish this account to any consumer reporting agency.

Be advised : * A generic agreement, blank forms, or documents that do not identify me specifically are insufficient.

* Reporting or attempting to collect without proper validation may constitute violations of federal law, including but not limited to 15 U.S.C. 1681 and 1692.

If you are unable to provide the requested documentation, you must : * Cease all collection activity * Remove this account from all consumer reporting agencies immediately Failure to comply will result in complaints filed with the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ), Federal Trade Commission ( FTC ), and my State Attorney General, as well as potential legal action.

This is not a refusal to pay, but a notice that your claim is disputed and must be validated. 
Sincerely, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX SS # XXXX",,"Portfolio Recovery Associates, LLC",GA,30253,,Web,2026-04-22,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
