21664650,2026-04-28,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"I am filing a complaint regarding the handling of a billing dispute on my Apple Card account ( issued by Goldman Sachs ). 

I disputed a charge for merchandise where the merchant refused to accept a return based on a final sale / no-return policy that was not clearly disclosed at the time of purchase. 
The item was discounted, but there was no indication on the product page or during checkout that the item was non-returnable or final sale. The only reference to this restriction appears buried within the merchants return policy page, which I was not required to acknowledge prior to completing the transaction. 

Because this material limitation was not clearly or conspicuously disclosed before payment, I did not have reasonable notice that the item could not be returned. I attempted to return the item promptly, but the merchant refused to accept it. 

Goldman Sachs denied my dispute on the basis that I did not return the merchandise in time. This is incorrect. I was not able to return the merchandise at all because the merchant refused to accept a return. 

My dispute should have been evaluated as a failure to disclose material terms or misrepresentation, not as a failure to return merchandise within a specified timeframe. 
I am requesting that Goldman Sachs : Reopen and properly evaluate my dispute under the correct reason code, and Provide a detailed explanation of how the merchants disclosure met applicable standards for clear and conspicuous notice of a no-return policy. 

I have supporting documentation, including screenshots of the checkout process showing no disclosure of a final sale condition, and written confirmation from the merchant refusing the return.",,GOLDMAN SACHS BANK USA,WI,53703,,Web,2026-04-28,Closed with explanation,Yes
21664794,2026-04-28,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers",Didn't receive advertised or promotional terms,"I am submitting this complaint regarding a promotional financing offer that was not honored on a purchase made through XXXX using my Chase credit card. 
On XX/XX/year>, I purchased a XXXX embroidery machine through XXXX. At the time of checkout, the purchase was presented with a 0 % promotional financing option. I made the purchase based on that offer. 
After the transaction posted, the promotional financing was not applied. Instead, the purchase was processed as a standard transaction with interest. 
I contacted Chase customer service multiple times and escalated the issue to a supervisor. I was ultimately told that the promotion would not be honored. However, I have documentation from XXXX confirming the promotional offer associated with my purchase. 
I made this purchase in good faith reliance on the 0 % financing terms presented at checkout. Had those terms not been offered, I would not have proceeded with the purchase under the same conditions. 
I am requesting that Chase : 1. Honor the 0 % promotional financing that was presented at the time of purchase, or 2. Provide a comparable resolution that reflects the originally advertised financing terms. 
I have attached documentation from XXXX supporting that the promotional offer was associated with my order. 
This situation appears to be a breakdown between XXXX and Chase systems, but as the consumer, I should not bear the financial impact of that error.",,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,LA,712XX,,Web,2026-04-28,Closed with explanation,Yes
