21708256,2026-04-29,Debt collection,Telecommunications debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt is not yours,"I am filing this complaint regarding collection activity from Sequium connected to ongoing XXXX XXXX account issues that have caused significant financial and credit harm. 

Issue 1 XXXX Charge-Off Related to Returned XXXX I am an over-the-road truck driver and originally purchased an XXXX from a XXXX store in Missouri. At the time, I wanted an XXXX XXXX XXXX, but the store only had a standard XXXX available. XXXX staff informed me that I could purchase the available phone and exchange it within the 30-day return period for the XXXX XXXX XXXX once it became available. 

Due to my busy trucking schedule, I later stopped at a XXXX store in XXXX, North Carolina, where I returned the original XXXX and completed the exchange/purchase for the XXXX XXXX XXXX. At the time, I believed everything was properly exchanged and resolved. 

Months later, XXXX began claiming there was still a balance owed for the returned phone. I attempted contacting both XXXX stores and customer service multiple times with little to no assistance. I was repeatedly redirected, spent countless hours on calls, and struggled to get a clear resolution. 

This issue eventually resulted in a XXXX charge-off appearing on my credit report with an alleged balance of approximately {$850.00}, which I dispute. I already submitted disputes with the credit bureaus without resolution, and there is currently an active dispute with XXXX and the credit bureaus directly. I am requesting this matter be fully investigated, including review of the returned device records, store transaction history, and exchange records. 

Issue 2 {$380.00} Collection Account Through Sequium After ongoing frustration with XXXX  customer service and account handling, I ultimately decided to cancel my XXXX service. Before canceling, I specifically asked the XXXX representative whether there would be any remaining balances or future charges after making my final payment. I made it very clear that I wanted to avoid another issue like the previous device dispute. 

The XXXX representative confidently informed me that I was fully paid and owed nothing further. 

Months later, I unexpectedly received a collection notice from Sequium regarding an alleged XXXX balance of {$380.00}. I was never properly informed beforehand that there was an outstanding balance or that the account would be referred to collections. 

Given the prior unresolved XXXX dispute and the fact that I directly confirmed with XXXX that my account was clear before cancellation, I am concerned about the validity and accuracy of the balance now being pursued through collections. 

I am requesting a full investigation into the XXXX account history, billing records, communications, and the validity of the alleged balance currently being pursued through Sequium collections. 

I am also requesting correction of any inaccurate reporting or improper collection activity associated with these matters to prevent further harm to my credit.",,"Sequium Asset Solutions, LLC",FL,XXXXX,,Web,2026-04-29,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
